.TH BIGFLOATRECIPROCAL 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatReciprocal, bigFloatDiv, bigFloatSqrt \- compute a reciprocal, quotient or square root
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

int bigFloatReciprocal(BigFloat *result, const BigFloat *x, size_t limbs);
int bigFloatDiv(BigFloat *result, const BigFloat *a, const BigFloat *b, size_t limbs);
int bigFloatSqrt(BigFloat *result, const BigFloat *x, size_t limbs);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These operations use an explicit positive size_t limb precision and store
that precision in the destination on success. One limb means 32 significant
binary bits. There is no fixed maximum precision setting.
.PP
Reciprocal computes one divided by x. Div computes a divided by b with scaled
exact integer long division. Sqrt uses a restoring integer square-root
algorithm. All round toward zero. Dynamic scratch is reserved before bit loops.
Output may alias either or both inputs. Inputs and output must be initialized.
Increasing requested precision cannot restore information lost from inputs.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0, -1 for allocation failure, INT_MAX for unrepresentable size/exponent,
or -2 for zero precision, a zero divisor, or a negative square-root sign
(including signed zero). Positive zero succeeds. Value and precision are
unchanged on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
